  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on `drv.motion.moving` after 3 of the 6 allowed runs. It reported 3 witnesses, 1 name, 1 atom read.\n\n- **Body:** `kin_speed x > speed_floor`. The comparison is strict because the contract says a speed at or below the floor counts as no motion. If the speed isn't observed, the body is unknown. No narrowing was needed.\n- **Witnesses:** they all use one eastbound lane, a car on track 1, and a speed floor of 0.1 m/s.\n  - **holds:** the car travels at 50 km/h.\n  - **fails:** the car stands still behind a stop line with zero speed.\n  - **blind:** the holds trace with `kin.speed` masked by the source.\n- **Gate runs:**\n  1. I ran the gate on the untouched skeletons by mistake. It returned `UNUSED_CLAIM`, which cost one run.\n  2. With the body written, it returned `WITNESS_FAIL` because the scenes were still the skeleton's empty ones.\n  3. With the scenes built, it returned `OK`.\n\nThe record looks consistent, so there's nothing to report back to the plan agent.\n\nFiles are in the working directory:\n- `/local-scratch2/sma407/smoke31-run/pipeline/traffic-spec-agent/library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/moving.lean`\n- `/local-scratch2/sma407/smoke31-run/pipeline/traffic-spec-agent/library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/motion/moving.lean`\n- `task_result.md`",
